      "id": "p1",
      "title": "Landing and stalemate",
      "time": "Days 1-5 before the battle (early September 490 BCE)",
      "durationSec": 8,
      "narration": "On Hippias's advice the Persians land in the Bay of Marathon. The Athenians march out and block the plain's two exits from the slopes of Mt Agrieliki, and Pheidippides runs to Sparta, which delays for the Carneia. A thousand Plataeans arrive. For about five days neither side attacks.",
